{
  "about": "The app's colour tokens, keyed by their CSS custom-property name. browser/css/theme.css is the SOURCE OF TRUTH and this file is generated from it — browser/tests/themeTokens.test.js re-derives it from the stylesheet and fails on any drift. The surfaces that cannot read CSS embed this instead of retyping hexes: desktop theme.cpp's Palette, the cli's logo/prompt colours.",
  "rules": {
    "keys": "The CSS custom-property name, verbatim (leading `--`), in theme.css declaration order.",
    "light": "The value declared in `:root`.",
    "dark": "The value declared in `[data-theme=\"dark\"]`, or the light value when that block omits the token — that is what the cascade gives.",
    "tokens": "Literal values only: a hex, an rgba(), a keyword, a shadow, or a url(). Safe to embed verbatim on any surface.",
    "derived": "COMPUTED tokens — the value names another token (`var(...)`) or mixes one (`color-mix(...)`), so it has no fixed hex. The EXPRESSION is recorded, never a resolved colour; a non-CSS surface must evaluate it against the accent in play (desktop theme.cpp accentShade(), cli setAccent()). Recording a resolved hex here would freeze the violet default and silently break every other accent.",
    "accents": "The 12 accent presets are NOT here — they live in accents.json, which every surface already reads.",
    "brand": "Theme-INDEPENDENT art colours (favicon.svg + the cli logo). Not CSS custom properties, so not pinned against theme.css; the favicon ones are pinned against favicon.svg."
  },
